# Keep text files LF in the working tree on every OS, not just Linux: the wire protocol,
# the export writers (newline="\n") and the byte-count assertions in the test suite all
# assume LF, so a CRLF checkout on Windows would break them.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary

# The exception: Windows batch interpreters need CRLF, and a .bat checked out with LF
# endings fails in ways that look nothing like a line-ending problem.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
